  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 922 PM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nHigh pressure will persist through the week, bringing \nwarm and dry conditions. Temperatures are expected to run 5-10 \ndegrees above normal through at least Friday.\n\nModels are coming into better agreement on a long-wave trough \nbringing several low pressure systems across the Western CONUS this \nweekend into next week. The first shortwave arrives Saturday with \nthe potential for colder temperatures along with valley rain and \nmountain snow. In general the snow levels appear to range from 7-9 \nkft, which is lower than previous storms. \n\nEarly next week, models are hinting at another shortwave moving \nthrough the region bringing another round of precipitation and \ncolder temperatures. Model agreement remains poor this far out, so \nbe sure to stay tuned to see how the forecast develops over the \ncoming days.",
